  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733936",
      "title": "Using Data From A Loader In The Route Component",
      "sourceHash": "f6b6165fb75421d70fed5d875eeae63484af3cb91d12a763fb07a0afe7c9eeda",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "So how do we now get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 7.05,
          "en": "to that data returned by our loader?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.05,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "Well, for that we have to go to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 11.19,
          "en": "where we want to use it. Like for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 15.48,
          "en": "the events page component. There, as a first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.48,
          "end": 18.15,
          "en": "I can get rid of all that remaining code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.15,
          "end": 21.09,
          "en": "which we had in there before, all that state management,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.09,
          "end": 24.3,
          "en": "and useEffect, and get rid of this div here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.3,
          "end": 26.97,
          "en": "which shows my loading and error estates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.97,
          "end": 30.39,
          "en": "We will see how we can implement those states again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.39,
          "end": 32.16,
          "en": "in the near future, but for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 35.04,
          "en": "we can get rid of that. Of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.04,
          "end": 36.78,
          "en": "we also get rid of these checks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.78,
          "end": 41.37,
          "en": "therefore and just return events list like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.37,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "and we can get rid of these imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.55,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "And now to get access to the data returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 49.08,
          "en": "by the loader function for this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.08,
          "end": 54.08,
          "en": "we can import \"use loader data\" from React-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.07,
          "end": 58.62,
          "en": "This is a special hook which we can execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.62,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "to get access to the closest loader data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 65.52,
          "en": "and I will show you what \"closest loader data\" means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.52,
          "end": 70.23,
          "en": "in just a second. So here, I now get my data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.23,
          "end": 73.14,
          "en": "by calling \"use loader data.\" We could also name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.14,
          "end": 75.53999999999999,
          "en": "it \"events\" since we know that it will be a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.53999999999999,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "of events in case of this component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 80.283,
          "en": "due to the code we wrote in this loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.6,
          "end": 84.3,
          "en": "And events here will really be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.3,
          "end": 86.373,
          "en": "that data returned by that loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.42,
          "end": 89.31,
          "en": "Now since I'm using a single weight,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.31,
          "end": 93.33,
          "en": "technically this loader function will return a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.33,
          "end": 95.85,
          "en": "Any data returned in that function will be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.85,
          "end": 99.24000000000001,
          "en": "by a promise, that's how a single weight works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.24000000000001,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "But React Router will actually check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 104.67,
          "en": "if a promise is returned and automatically get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.67,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "the resolved data from that promise for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 109.11,
          "en": "So you don't need to worry about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.11,
          "end": 111.75,
          "en": "whether you are returning a promise here or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.75,
          "end": 115.38,
          "en": "you will always get the final data that would be yielded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.38,
          "end": 118.563,
          "en": "by the promise with help of use loader data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.64,
          "end": 122.88,
          "en": "And therefore now it's this events object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 126.03,
          "en": "this array of events, which we can pass as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.03,
          "end": 128.553,
          "en": "to this events prop on events list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.96,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "If we save that all, you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 134.04,
          "en": "that we got the same result as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.04,
          "end": 137.1,
          "en": "we got this list of events, in this case only one event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.1,
          "end": 139.74,
          "en": "but if we had multiple events returned by the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.74,
          "end": 141.663,
          "en": "we would see multiple events here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.89,
          "end": 147.06,
          "en": "And we got this all due to the code we wrote in this loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.06,
          "end": 150.06,
          "en": "And of course that's much less code than what we had before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.06,
          "end": 152.55,
          "en": "and it's also not part of the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.55,
          "end": 155.01,
          "en": "which makes the component function way leaner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.01,
          "end": 158.19,
          "en": "and easier to reason about. Of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.19,
          "end": 161.64,
          "en": "we're also not managing any loading or error estate yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.64,
          "end": 165.18,
          "en": "but nonetheless we got a way leaner events page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.18,
          "end": 167.64,
          "en": "and that's definitely a decent improvement over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.64,
          "end": 168.873,
          "en": "what we had before.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}